The pair product is local: for odd q, midpoint residues m=+/-h mod q are forbidden.
If q divides h, two forbidden residues collapse to one, creating the HL boost.

================================================================================================================
MIDPOINT SIEVE: TWIN PRIMES ARE SURVIVORS OF +/-1
================================================================================================================
   h forbidden residues m mod q                                     finite survival
   1 q=3:[1, 2]; q=5:[1, 4]; q=7:[1, 6]; q=11:[1, 10]; q=13:[1, 12] 9/91
   2 q=3:[1, 2]; q=5:[2, 3]; q=7:[2, 5]; q=11:[2, 9]; q=13:[2, 11]  9/91
   3 q=3:[0]; q=5:[2, 3]; q=7:[3, 4]; q=11:[3, 8]; q=13:[3, 10]     18/91
   5 q=3:[1, 2]; q=5:[0]; q=7:[2, 5]; q=11:[5, 6]; q=13:[5, 8]      12/91
   6 q=3:[0]; q=5:[1, 4]; q=7:[1, 6]; q=11:[5, 6]; q=13:[6, 7]      18/91
  15 q=3:[0]; q=5:[0]; q=7:[1, 6]; q=11:[4, 7]; q=13:[2, 11]        24/91

For twin primes beyond (3,5), h=1 forces m divisible by 2 and 3,
so the midpoint lives on the 6Z spine: (6k-1, 6k+1).

